{{!-- META {"path":"parallax","title":"Parallax","description":"Scroll-linked movement, fading, scaling and blur, written as attributes on any element. Each effect runs over its own window of the element's pass through the screen, and none of it runs for visitors who prefer reduced motion.","parent":"showcase","order":10,"data":{"icon":"stack","preset":"drifting-blobs"}} --}}
{{> page-hero parent=page.parent}}

<section class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-6 py-16 sm:py-24">
  <div class="max-w-3xl" data-sw-animation="fade-up">
    <p class="ws-index ws-ink">01 · A depth scene</p>
    <h2 class="ws-display mt-3 text-3xl font-bold sm:text-5xl" data-sw-text="p1_title">Scroll through this one slowly.</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-lg leading-relaxed text-base-content/70" data-sw-text="p1_lead">A scene clips a stack of layers that move on their own. The background layer drifts and eases its zoom. The content layer rises, fades in, grows and sharpens until it reaches the middle of the screen, then eases back out. It is marked <code class="font-code text-base">content</code>, so it stays in the flow and gives the scene its height.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="mt-10">
<!--demo:scene-->
<div data-sw-parallax-scene class="min-h-[30rem] rounded-3xl bg-neutral text-white">
  <div data-sw-parallax-layer data-sw-parallax-translate="60,-60" data-sw-parallax-scale="1.3,1.15" class="bg-gradient-to-br from-primary via-neutral to-accent opacity-80"></div>
  <div data-sw-parallax-layer="content"
       data-sw-parallax-translate="40,-40"
       data-sw-parallax-opacity="0,1" data-sw-parallax-opacity-range="0,0.5" data-sw-parallax-opacity-out="1,0"
       data-sw-parallax-scale="0.85,1" data-sw-parallax-scale-range="0,0.5" data-sw-parallax-scale-out="1,1.06"
       data-sw-parallax-blur="10,0" data-sw-parallax-blur-range="0,0.5" data-sw-parallax-blur-out="0,6"
       class="grid min-h-[30rem] place-items-center px-6 text-center">
    <div>
      <p class="ws-display text-4xl font-bold sm:text-6xl">Depth, from attributes.</p>
      <p class="mx-auto mt-4 max-w-xl text-lg text-white/80">Translate, opacity, scale and blur, each with its own window and an out phase.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
<!--/demo-->
  </div>
  <div class="mt-6">
<!--code:scene file="parallax · depth scene"-->
  </div>
</section>

<section class="border-y border-base-content/10 bg-base-200/50">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-6 py-16 sm:py-24">
    <div class="max-w-3xl" data-sw-animation="fade-up">
      <p class="ws-index ws-ink">02 · Movement</p>
      <h2 class="ws-display mt-3 text-3xl font-bold sm:text-5xl" data-sw-text="p2_title">From one offset to another.</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-lg leading-relaxed text-base-content/70" data-sw-text="p2_lead"><code class="font-code text-base">data-sw-parallax-translate="from,to"</code> moves an element between two pixel offsets while it crosses the screen. A bigger range feels closer. Opposite directions read as depth, and <code class="font-code text-base">data-sw-parallax-axis="x"</code> moves it sideways.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="mt-12 grid grid-cols-1 gap-6 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4">
<!--demo:translate-->
<div data-sw-parallax-translate="90,-90" class="rounded-3xl border border-base-content/10 bg-base-100 p-8 text-center shadow-lg">
  <p class="ws-numeral text-5xl">90 → −90</p>
  <p class="mt-3 ws-index text-base-content/60">near</p>
</div>
<div class="rounded-3xl border border-base-content/10 bg-base-100 p-8 text-center shadow-lg">
  <p class="ws-numeral text-5xl">0</p>
  <p class="mt-3 ws-index text-base-content/60">still</p>
</div>
<div data-sw-parallax-translate="-30,30" class="rounded-3xl border border-base-content/10 bg-base-100 p-8 text-center shadow-lg">
  <p class="ws-numeral text-5xl">−30 → 30</p>
  <p class="mt-3 ws-index text-base-content/60">far</p>
</div>
<div data-sw-parallax-translate="-40,40" data-sw-parallax-axis="x" class="rounded-3xl border border-base-content/10 bg-base-100 p-8 text-center shadow-lg">
  <p class="ws-numeral text-5xl">x axis</p>
  <p class="mt-3 ws-index text-base-content/60">sideways</p>
</div>
<!--/demo-->
    </div>
    <div class="mt-10">
<!--code:translate file="parallax · translate"-->
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-6 py-16 sm:py-24">
  <div class="max-w-3xl" data-sw-animation="fade-up">
    <p class="ws-index ws-ink">03 · Fade, scale, blur</p>
    <h2 class="ws-display mt-3 text-3xl font-bold sm:text-5xl" data-sw-text="p3_title">More channels, same grammar.</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-lg leading-relaxed text-base-content/70" data-sw-text="p3_lead">Opacity, scale and blur each take a from,to pair too, and they combine on one element. Blur costs the most to draw, so use it sparingly.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="mt-10 grid grid-cols-1 gap-6 sm:grid-cols-3">
<!--demo:channels-->
<div data-sw-parallax-opacity="0.1,1" class="rounded-3xl bg-gradient-to-br from-primary to-secondary p-8 font-heading text-xl font-bold text-white">Fades in as it rises</div>
<div data-sw-parallax-scale="0.85,1.05" class="rounded-3xl bg-gradient-to-br from-primary to-secondary p-8 font-heading text-xl font-bold text-white">Grows as it rises</div>
<div data-sw-parallax-blur="8,0" class="rounded-3xl bg-gradient-to-br from-primary to-secondary p-8 font-heading text-xl font-bold text-white">Comes into focus</div>
<!--/demo-->
  </div>
  <div class="mt-6">
<!--code:channels file="parallax · opacity, scale, blur"-->
  </div>
</section>

<section class="border-y border-base-content/10 bg-base-200/50">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-6 py-16 sm:py-24">
    <div class="max-w-3xl" data-sw-animation="fade-up">
      <p class="ws-index ws-ink">04 · Windows</p>
      <h2 class="ws-display mt-3 text-3xl font-bold sm:text-5xl" data-sw-text="p4_title">Finish in the middle, then leave.</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-lg leading-relaxed text-base-content/70" data-sw-text="p4_lead">An effect runs over the whole pass by default, so it peaks as the element leaves the top. A window of <code class="font-code text-base">0,0.5</code> finishes it when the element is centred. The rest of the pass is then free for an <code class="font-code text-base">-out</code> phase: in, hold, out.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="mt-10 grid grid-cols-1 gap-6 sm:grid-cols-2">
<!--demo:windows-->
<div data-sw-parallax-opacity="0,1" data-sw-parallax-opacity-range="0,0.5" class="rounded-3xl bg-neutral p-8 font-heading text-xl font-bold text-white">Fully visible by the centre</div>
<div data-sw-parallax-opacity="0,1" data-sw-parallax-opacity-range="0,0.5" data-sw-parallax-opacity-out="1,0" data-sw-parallax-scale="0.9,1" data-sw-parallax-scale-range="0,0.5" data-sw-parallax-scale-out="1,0.9" class="rounded-3xl bg-neutral p-8 font-heading text-xl font-bold text-white">In to the centre, then back out</div>
<!--/demo-->
    </div>
    <div class="mt-6">
<!--code:windows file="parallax · windows"-->
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-6 py-16 sm:py-24">
  <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-6 md:grid-cols-3">
    <div class="rounded-3xl border border-base-content/10 bg-base-100 p-6" data-sw-animation="fade-up">
      {{sw-icon "person-simple" "h-6 w-6 ws-ink"}}
      <h3 class="mt-4 font-heading text-lg font-bold">Reduced motion</h3>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-base-content/70">For visitors who ask for less motion the runtime does nothing at all, and every element sits where the layout put it.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="rounded-3xl border border-base-content/10 bg-base-100 p-6" data-sw-animation="fade-up" data-sw-delay="80">
      {{sw-icon "layout" "h-6 w-6 ws-ink"}}
      <h3 class="mt-4 font-heading text-lg font-bold">Never moves the layout</h3>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-base-content/70">The runtime only adds a transform, an opacity or a filter. Without JavaScript nothing shifts, overlaps or disappears.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="rounded-3xl border border-base-content/10 bg-base-100 p-6" data-sw-animation="fade-up" data-sw-delay="160">
      {{sw-icon "sliders-horizontal" "h-6 w-6 ws-ink"}}
      <h3 class="mt-4 font-heading text-lg font-bold">A builder in the editor</h3>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-base-content/70">The editor's Library has a Parallax builder that writes these attributes for you, with a live preview.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{{> showcase-next}}
